{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>וישמע.</b> The land of Midian was under the dominion of Pharaoh; therefore he needed to be a shepherd of sheep so that he would not stay in a settled place, lest they recognize him. And when HaShem told him that Pharaoh and the servants from whom he had fled had died, and his younger son was born in those days, then he said, ויצילני מחרב פרעה (Exodus 18:4), for all the days of his life he feared him. And after he mentioned וישב בארץ מדין, he returned to explain why he stayed: for at first he stayed by the known well, in the manner of ויצא יעקב… וילך (Genesis 28:10), and he returned to mean ויפגע במקום (ibid. 11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:04.531624911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}